This is a basic Java written program that conducts CRUD (create, read, update, delete) opertations
And involves a connection to postgress or Pgadmin4

Postgress database creation scripts
CREATE TABLE students (
    student_id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    first_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    last_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    enrollment_date DATE
);

INSERT INTO students (first_name, last_name, email, enrollment_date) VALUES
('John', 'Doe', 'john.doe@example.com', '2023-09-01'),
('Jane', 'Smith', 'jane.smith@example.com', '2023-09-01'),
('Jim', 'Beam', 'jim.beam@example.com', '2023-09-02');

1: To actually run this program you must have postgress installed and have the program running with the database created
2: You must then change the final part (Assignment3) this line in the code:
    private final String url = "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/Assignment3";
    to instead connect to whatever the name of the database you are using
3: from there you also have to put in your username and password within the following lines
    private final String user = "postgres";
    private final String password = "password";
4: you then run the program and you are able to do the CRUD operations as long as they follow the prepared statements

